The digit recognizer weights (backend/hwr/model.bin) were trained by
hwrtrain/ on the following datasets. The datasets are not included in this
repository.

- MNIST. Y. LeCun, C. Cortes, C. J. C. Burges. Derived from NIST Special
  Databases 1 and 3. No explicit license is published with the files; it is
  commonly redistributed under CC BY-SA 3.0.
- EMNIST (letters, used only as "not a digit" examples). G. Cohen,
  S. Afshar, J. Tapson, A. van Schaik, "EMNIST: an extension of MNIST to
  handwritten letters", 2017. Derived from NIST Special Database 19.
- Pen-Based Recognition of Handwritten Digits. E. Alpaydin, F. Alimoglu.
  UCI Machine Learning Repository, dataset 81. CC BY 4.0.
- UJI Pen Characters (Version 2). D. Llorens et al. UCI Machine Learning
  Repository, dataset 177. Version 1 (dataset 160) is CC BY 4.0; the terms
  of version 2 could not be confirmed when the model was trained.

The apps draw text in EB Garamond (SIL Open Font License 1.1), which ships
with the reMarkable system software and is not included here.

Ink Sudoku runs inside AppLoad by asivery (https://github.com/asivery/rm-appload);
no AppLoad code is included. Its message protocol was implemented from
documentation and observed behaviour (see PROTOCOL.md).
